Every value is greater than 1, so no floor exists.
Complexity
- Time: \(O(h)\) — at most one path through the BST is explored.
- Auxiliary space: \(O(1)\) — only a few variables are used.
A balanced BST gives \(O(\log n)\) time; a skewed BST can take \(O(n)\) time.

