7. Interview memory trick: Floor vs. Ceil
Condition at current node	Floor in BST	Ceil in BST
Exact match	Return current value	Return current value
Current value is smaller than target	Save candidate; go right	Go right
Current value is greater than target	Go left	Save candidate; go left

The key difference is the direction in which you save a candidate:
- Floor: save smaller valid values and search right for a bigger one.
- Ceil: save larger valid values and search left for a smaller one.
Final verdict: Your iterative findMaxFork solution is the most optimal of these approaches in auxiliary space. It uses the BST property, takes \(O(h)\) time, and requires \(O(1)\) extra space.
